1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:03,880
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:45,520
[DERA]
I'm so drinkin' on his tab.

3
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:46,520
Hm?

4
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:51,150
Well...

5
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:53,200
[Dera smirks]

6
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,870
We're already here,
in the middle of the city.

7
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,700
Might as well have some fun!

8
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,160
Time for a lesson.

9
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,960
[YURU AND RIGHT] Uh?

10
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,420
[DERA] You're gonna learn
about the world!

11
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:09,670
[Right yells]

12
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:12,170
[Yuru exclaiming]

13
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,930
[Yuru laughs]

14
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:16,840
[Right exclaiming]

15
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:19,640
[Yuru exclaiming]

16
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,850
[Right cheering]

17
00:02:21,930 --> 00:02:22,850
[MAN] Uh?

18
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:25,770
[crowd cheering]

19
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:27,730
[Dera cheering]

20
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:30,650
Pick up the pace!

21
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,650
[Dera groans softly]

22
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:40,330
[YURU] The horses down here
are huge, and so fast!

23
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,080
Riding them must take practice.

24
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,830
Really liked the one
that finished in first place.

25
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,750
I wonder how much it would cost.

26
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:49,210
Please, no.
Hana would divorce me.

27
00:02:49,290 --> 00:02:51,090
But if you want
something reasonable,

28
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,090
let me know.

29
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,010
Horses, cattle.

30
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:55,430
Forget the livestock.

31
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:59,720
[YURU] Besides that, the thing
I need most would be arrows.

32
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:01,600
I've only got
a bow at your place.

33
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,810
Nothing to fire.

34
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:04,640
Yeah, that's tricky.

35
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:06,400
Where do they sell arrows?

36
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:09,060
I could craft my own,
if I had the materials.

37
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:11,070
[DERA] Uh? Hmm.

38
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:16,530
[Yuru and Right exclaiming]

39
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:19,370
You mean
all of this is for sale?

40
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:20,620
Yup.

41
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,410
[DERA] What do you need
to make arrows?

42
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,000
[YURU] Some bamboo,
thread, and a knife.

43
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,460
And something hard
for the arrowheads.

44
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,000
[DERA] What about fletching?

45
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:31,710
[YURU] We've got
the feathers from the pheasant

46
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:33,050
I sold you the other day.

47
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,420
Think we can get an entire deer?

48
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:36,470
What?

49
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:39,510
I can boil the skin and organs
to fix myself up some glue.

50
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:41,180
And how would that smell?

51
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,470
We'd get complaints
from our neighbors.

52
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,720
-Use this.
-[YURU] Uh?

53
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:49,440
-[DERA] Introducing, wood glue!
-[YURU] What does that mean?

54
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,400
[DERA] Here, check it out.

55
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:53,190
[YURU] That's so convenient!

56
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,690
[CLERK] Next customer!

57
00:03:56,690 --> 00:03:59,030
They really have
everything down here.

58
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,160
[clerk stammers]

59
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:09,540
A one. A two. A three.

60
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:13,210
Thank you, have a nice day.

61
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,130
Hey, boss.

62
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:19,130
I seem to be hallucinating.
Can I have a break?

63
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:22,430
What? Quit screwing around
and get back to work.

64
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:24,930
[CLERK] I hate this job!

65
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:26,480
That's peculiar.

66
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,980
Seems the lass with
the beeping device could see us.

67
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,650
If she were a Daemon Wielder,
we would smell them on her.

68
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:33,650
It's like you said before.

69
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:35,520
Some people just have the sight.

70
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:38,400
It can also happen when
someone's badly sleep-deprived.

71
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,320
We should get you
some clothes, too.

72
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,280
[Yuru gasps]

73
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:46,950
A scarecrow?

74
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:50,370
Huh.

75
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,460
I like that
the clothes down here

76
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,210
have many storage compartments.

77
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:56,380
Yep! Grab what you like!

78
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,590
I prefer wearing black.

79
00:04:58,670 --> 00:05:01,050
It makes bloodstains easier
to hide.

80
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:03,180
[DERA] Oh, good, he's basing
his fashion choices

81
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,680
on blood splatter!

82
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,560
-Need some boxers?
-[YURU] Some what?

83
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,140
[DERA] A kind of underpants.
They're like loincloths.

84
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:11,060
[YURU]
I'll stick with what I know.

85
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,230
I don't like these.

86
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:13,980
[Dera chuckles softly]
Excuse me.

87
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:15,440
Do you have loincloths?

88
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:17,530
I'm afraid not. Only those.

89
00:05:17,610 --> 00:05:20,070
-Oh... That's right.
-[DERA] Hm?

90
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:22,950
This reminded me
of when I would go hunting.

91
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,910
At times, bandits would attack
when I was by myself.

92
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:28,660
And just like
my father taught me,

93
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,660
if I thought
they wanted to kill me,

94
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,830
I'd kill first in response.

95
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:35,380
Even after I buried them
or sent them downstream,

96
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,130
something always felt off.

97
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,630
Now, I can finally say
what that was.

98
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:42,930
These bandits weren't young,

99
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:44,800
but their hands were so clean.

100
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:46,810
Where I come from,

101
00:05:46,890 --> 00:05:49,060
the labor means
you're gonna get dirty.

102
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,480
And past a certain age,
the dirt really settles in.

103
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:55,650
So nails and knuckles
can't be washed clean.

104
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,310
They were like you.

105
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,650
Their hands were
in good condition

106
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,820
because they lived
in a place that allowed it.

107
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,440
But now I see why.

108
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:05,200
And why they were wearing
these boxer things.

109
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,160
Did you strip them?

110
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,580
The bandits came up there
to kill me.

111
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,500
Someone sent them
to the mountain as assassins.

112
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,290
They would've lost your trust

113
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:15,750
if you came back
after a villager

114
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,290
you knew took your life.

115
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,710
This way, you'd believe
you gained the power of Seal

116
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,550
after an outsider cut you down.

117
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:24,260
Their hold on you
would be all the stronger.

118
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:25,630
We don't know for certain

119
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,050
that it was the village
who sent them.

120
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:31,060
But I can't trust them
anymore, either.

121
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:32,770
What if something happened
in the mountains

122
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,480
while you were by yourself,
huh?

123
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,480
Even though I want to.

124
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:40,900
The barrier to Higashi Village
is not an easy code to crack.

125
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,530
There's only a few besides me
who could.

126
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:45,070
How nice.

127
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:47,030
That narrows it down.

128
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:49,740
Shall we lay a trap for them?

129
00:06:49,830 --> 00:06:52,410
[YURU] Yeah.
Better to take the initiative.

130
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,540
I thought you might say that.

131
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,630
[YURU] The winner
of the hunt is the one

132
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:58,380
with the best positioning.

133
00:06:59,170 --> 00:07:01,550
-Speaking of which, Dera...
-Yeah?

134
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:03,800
We're being followed.

135
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,090
I know. I count three.

136
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:08,800
[YURU] One, two, three.

137
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:11,060
And they're taking turns
tailing us.

138
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:13,270
Think they're Kagemori guys?

139
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:15,520
Man, they're pieces of work.

140
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,230
Don't look behind you.

141
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:20,110
Understood. Uh, hold on.

142
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,400
You told me you didn't want them
to find you,

143
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:24,530
but you were in that painting?

144
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,610
The thing Asa's device made.

145
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,740
Wouldn't they be able
to use that to identify you?

146
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:31,080
[DERA] Eh, too late.

147
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,830
Rich people can shell out
for security cameras

148
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:35,160
all over their mansions.

149
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:38,380
[YURU] Shell out?

150
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:41,210
I knew when I arrived,
they'd have my face.

151
00:07:41,290 --> 00:07:44,210
Had to write that off
as the cost for picking you up.

152
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,300
[ASA] The two of us.

153
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,930
[Asa laughs]

154
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,680
Hmm.

155
00:07:57,390 --> 00:08:00,690
[ASA] Now where's that
photo editing app?

156
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:02,900
There.

157
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:05,690
Asa, did you get
a picture of Tadera?

158
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,320
We'd like to see it.

159
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:09,360
He wasn't in the frame.

160
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:11,280
He's potentially dangerous.

161
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:12,990
Your information will help.

162
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,490
Wait. He's not?

163
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,910
Afraid not.

164
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,210
He wasn't in the one you took
of your brother?

165
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:19,670
Afraid not.

166
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:22,920
Haruo,
check the security camera.

167
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
We'll take anything
we've got on him.

168
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,550
And if you find any footage
of my brother, I'll take it!

169
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:31,090
[Jin sighs]

170
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,850
[HAMURA] I mentioned
the bearded guy

171
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:36,010
in the camo jacket.
Name's Akishima.

172
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,060
And he's the one you go to
for work on the down low.

173
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:40,730
Contacted us same as usual

174
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:42,520
for a job with pay
through the roof.

175
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:44,940
[TACHIKAWA]
This is my call history.

176
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:47,320
He reached out yesterday
at midnight to explain

177
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,820
what this gig would entail.

178
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:51,780
Timing lines up perfectly
on my phone, too.

179
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:52,910
[GONZO] Hmm.

180
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,410
[TACHIKAWA] I figure he must've
just called everyone in the area

181
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:56,910
who could get there fast.

182
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,580
[HAMURA]
It's like I told you before.

183
00:08:58,660 --> 00:08:59,790
None of us on the team

184
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:01,620
met each other
till we got there.

185
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:03,500
[HARUO] Midnight, huh?

186
00:09:03,590 --> 00:09:05,750
Exactly when we finished up
our fight with Yuru

187
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,130
and were driving back
to the manor.

188
00:09:07,210 --> 00:09:08,840
I'm checking my own logs,

189
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,220
and it seems like that's
when Jin called me, too.

190
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,140
About what time did you actually
enter the manor?

191
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,470
It was definitely after 1:30,
but before 2:00 a.m.

192
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,180
[SAKURAZAWA]
Right when you came to me

193
00:09:19,270 --> 00:09:21,440
-to get your leg treated.
-[JIN] Seems so.

194
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,230
[GONZO] We have this manor
surrounded by a barrier.

195
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:26,730
At that time of night,
the only ones who should be

196
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,820
able to enter
are members of the family

197
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,490
and those they invite in.

198
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:33,240
If there was a Kagemori
at the gate who invited you in,

199
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,700
we'd like to know who,

200
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:37,410
so we can prevent
future internal transgressions.

201
00:09:37,490 --> 00:09:40,660
Beardy... Akishima was
the only person we saw.

202
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:42,960
Actually, the west gate
was open,

203
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,380
and we walked in
with no problem.

204
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,790
Yeah, good point.

205
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:48,420
We were told the manor
was full of daemons,

206
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,260
so we just needed to get inside.

207
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,220
After that,
blending in was no problem.

208
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,720
Hold on there.
Which gate did you say again?

209
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,470
What? The west gate.

210
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,520
The west side of the manor
doesn't have a gate

211
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,810
you could've gone through.

212
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:02,980
Huh?

213
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,560
No? It does!

214
00:10:04,650 --> 00:10:06,360
You're wrong.

215
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:09,190
The entire west side is a wall.

216
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:11,150
There's no place
you could've entered.

217
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:13,320
Much less
without drawing attention.

218
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,700
[both gasp]

219
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,120
Fuyuki.

220
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,280
Sir.

221
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:21,410
[gasping]

222
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,540
Stop! What are you gonna do
to my partners?

223
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,250
Chill out, dude.
Fuyuki isn't going to kill 'em.

224
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:30,130
This pair is known
as Kori-Henge.

225
00:10:30,210 --> 00:10:31,970
Their master gave them
personal names.

226
00:10:32,050 --> 00:10:34,680
This is Akai and Midori.

227
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:37,350
Their current master
is Makoto Tachikawa.

228
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:40,640
She was born on May 4th,
in the year 1997.

229
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:43,480
She's a dropout
at Ariake Women's U.

230
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:46,230
She resides in Shinkiba,
Koto-ku, Tokyo.

231
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:49,270
She has one sister
and has one brother.

232
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:52,400
Parents...
Divorced in August, 2008.

233
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:54,570
Her mother won
full custody of her,

234
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:56,570
though she is now
in the hospital.

235
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,660
Subject is currently unemployed.

236
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,030
-She accepted this job...
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!

237
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,790
-...to help pay for her--
-Ah, pardon me.

238
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,250
It doesn't seem right of me

239
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:06,210
to expose a lady's
personal information like that.

240
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,170
Wrong for a guy, too.

241
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,340
Whisper, could you
cease speaking for a moment?

242
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:12,670
As you wish.

243
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:16,300
[FUYUKI] Hmm.

244
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:18,180
-[Tachikawa whimpers]
-[FUYUKI] Ah, yes, good.

245
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:19,350
What the hell was that?

246
00:11:19,430 --> 00:11:21,850
The next one please, embrace.

247
00:11:22,470 --> 00:11:23,640
[Daifuku and Ohagi grunting]

248
00:11:23,730 --> 00:11:25,600
[ASA]
Please be gentle with them.

249
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,600
I am never anything but gentle.

250
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,150
Pair name, Yin-Yang.

251
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:31,520
No personal names.

252
00:11:31,610 --> 00:11:33,610
Their current master is Asa.

253
00:11:33,690 --> 00:11:36,320
Their previous master
is Kenichi Hamura.

254
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:40,450
He was born on the 16th of June,
in the year 1992.

255
00:11:40,530 --> 00:11:42,450
-[trembling]
-[FUYUKI] Current residence...

256
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:44,660
Yes. Got it.

257
00:11:44,750 --> 00:11:47,660
I see. Debt from your gambling.

258
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,080
Both of them told us the truth.

259
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:52,250
They really did meet
on site for this job.

260
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:55,670
Who is this dude trampling
all over Japan's privacy laws?

261
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,800
[FUYUKI] Fuyuki Kuroya.

262
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:00,640
As for my daemon pair,
you may call them Blacklist.

263
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,220
They can extract information

264
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,560
on a daemon's master,
past or present.

265
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,810
And one touch is all it takes.

266
00:12:06,890 --> 00:12:09,140
Now that we know
you really are just mercs

267
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:12,230
and there's no lingering
affiliations to worry about...

268
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,530
if you're struggling for money,
you can have a job, with us!

269
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:17,700
[BOTH] Huh?

270
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,360
Well, I don't wanna sound like

271
00:12:19,450 --> 00:12:21,450
I don't appreciate
your kindness.

272
00:12:21,530 --> 00:12:23,620
But you're not gonna kill us?

273
00:12:24,830 --> 00:12:27,080
I'll just work you until
you wish you were dead!

274
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,710
[both whimper]

275
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,580
[GONZO]
Your mother's hospital bills...

276
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:31,670
Are they expensive?

277
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:34,630
Oh, um... Yes, very...

278
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:36,670
I'll front you the cost
of everything.

279
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,220
Tell your mother to rest easy

280
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,300
and to devote herself
to feeling better.

281
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,050
[TACHIKAWA]
Thank you so much, sir!

282
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,890
Any chance you could
front me some... [grunts]

283
00:12:44,970 --> 00:12:48,180
You can work off your debts
the slow and steady way!

284
00:12:48,270 --> 00:12:52,060
To start, the manor is
an absolute mess! Clean it!

285
00:12:52,150 --> 00:12:54,520
[TACHIKAWA AND HAMURA]
Oh! Yes, sir!

286
00:12:56,230 --> 00:12:58,150
[NATSUKI] Are you sure
they're safe to leave alive?

287
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,490
[GONZO] It's fine.

288
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,950
We know who they are
and where they live,

289
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:03,370
among other details.

290
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:05,120
And it never hurts to have

291
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:07,160
some more cannon fodder
on our staff.

292
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:08,870
Of course, sir.

293
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,210
And what should we do

294
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:12,630
with the other Daemon Wielders
we captured?

295
00:13:12,710 --> 00:13:15,090
For the ones whose daemons
died in the battle,

296
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,920
force them into contracts
with new ones later.

297
00:13:18,010 --> 00:13:21,880
After that, use Blacklist
to get their information.

298
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:26,600
If you do figure out
who the mastermind is,

299
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,770
round them up with everyone
they're associated with

300
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,930
and kill them.

301
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:32,730
[NATSUKI] We're on it, sir.

302
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:36,150
-[birds chirping]
-[sweeping]

303
00:13:42,950 --> 00:13:44,620
[HAMURA] Excuse me, miss.

304
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:48,120
Is there any chance you could
give me those daemons back?

305
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,620
I will consider it.
Did you name them yet?

306
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:52,830
Oh, uh...

307
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:55,880
Daifuku. Ohagi.

308
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:58,250
What?

309
00:13:59,050 --> 00:14:01,300
-[Gabby and Asa laugh]
-[ASA] Like the snacks?

310
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,670
Oh, that's adorable!

311
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,550
What's the big deal?
I like sweets, okay?

312
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,800
Wouldn't expect
such peaceful names from a guy

313
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:09,510
who acts as tough as you do.

314
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:10,730
[HAMURA] Give me a break!

315
00:14:10,810 --> 00:14:12,520
Says the guy
who named his daemons

316
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,690
after the words
for love and sincerity.

317
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,860
Like those teeth of yours
have some awesome name?

318
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:18,020
Of course!

319
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,690
One is Joe William
Frederic Gabriel the First,

320
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:21,940
and the other one is

321
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:24,320
Kirk Douglas Auldglaive Gabriel
the Second!

322
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,370
Great.

323
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,490
You don't think those names
are too much of a mouthful?

324
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:28,660
[Gabby grunts]

325
00:14:28,990 --> 00:14:31,250
-[Gabriel growls]
-[HAMURA] Sorry, sorry, sorry...

326
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:34,080
Well?
The apology did seem legit.

327
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,130
And he gave you guys
a couple of cute names.

328
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:37,460
Would you like
to go back to him?

329
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:39,920
[both grunting]

330
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,800
[ASA] That's a no.

331
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,170
[Hamura groans]

332
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,930
They know it takes
more than a night

333
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:46,720
for someone's mind to change.

334
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,050
It's fine. I can take care
of them for now.

335
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,930
Get back to work.

336
00:14:51,010 --> 00:14:52,060
[Hamura groans]

337
00:14:52,770 --> 00:14:54,180
Break isn't giving you
any trouble

338
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:55,770
keeping around your new friends?

339
00:14:55,850 --> 00:14:59,070
Nah. Haven't heard
a single peep out of that one.

340
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:01,270
I guess we're compatible
with Yin and Yang.

341
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:04,450
Then why not just let 'em
stay contracted to you forever?

342
00:15:04,530 --> 00:15:07,280
The more eyes watchin' over you,
the safer you are.

343
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:09,830
Hm. You've got a point.

344
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,700
There could still be enemies
lying in wait

345
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:14,460
right under our noses.

346
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,960
[WOMAN ON SPEAKERS]
That was too close for comfort.

347
00:15:22,050 --> 00:15:23,550
[HAGURE] Yeah.

348
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:26,380
I panicked when
things didn't go to plan.

349
00:15:26,470 --> 00:15:28,970
Sorry for the trouble
that caused you, Nakagami.

350
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:30,800
I'll do better next time.

351
00:15:30,890 --> 00:15:32,060
[NAKAGAMI]
About next time...

352
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,980
Should we try hiring
more people?

353
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:36,890
If you're fine with part-timers,
I've got quite a few.

354
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,480
They're ready to go right now.

355
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,230
[HAGURE] No. I don't need
more warm bodies.

356
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,440
Gabby and Asa have potential.

357
00:15:43,530 --> 00:15:45,900
I believe I can make
good use of them.

358
00:15:45,990 --> 00:15:48,280
[NAKAGAMI]
You'll be okay without backup?

359
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:51,620
Yes. Or I'll figure it out.

360
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,040
But seriously,

361
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,410
I thought for sure I was gonna
miss my deadline this time!

362
00:15:57,460 --> 00:16:00,840
Whoo, boy.
I have never been so scared!

363
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,800
All my assistants got sick
at the same time!

364
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,300
Then when my files
got corrupted,

365
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,880
I was so behind schedule,
I panicked!

366
00:16:07,970 --> 00:16:10,300
Yeah, that was almost
a total disaster.

367
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:13,350
And getting the printer
last minute? I had to beg!

368
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:15,350
I am so sorry for the trouble.

369
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:18,100
I'll manage my schedule
better next time.

370
00:16:18,190 --> 00:16:20,770
But I really am fine
without more assistants.

371
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:22,650
Gabby and Asa
have been a great help.

372
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:24,150
They've been putting
the finishing touches

373
00:16:24,230 --> 00:16:25,150
on my pages!

374
00:16:25,230 --> 00:16:27,530
Aw! You always talk about

375
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:29,070
how proud you are
of those girls.

376
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:30,490
They're such sweet kids.

377
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:32,700
You better be paying them
for all that work.

378
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:34,780
Well, of course I am!

379
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,160
[NAKAGAMI] Also,
what's going on over there?

380
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,210
Why are all the lights
in your room off?

381
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:42,170
Are you trying to play the boss
of some evil organization

382
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:43,710
-or something?
-[Hagure laughs]

383
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:45,500
[HAGURE] No!
Our house got damaged,

384
00:16:45,590 --> 00:16:47,220
and some parts
still don't have power!

385
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:51,050
Perfect.

386
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:53,680
Way easier to move in
than those sandal things.

387
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:58,270
They're still on us.

388
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:01,140
[DERA] Not like a simple change
of clothes was gonna shake 'em.

389
00:17:01,230 --> 00:17:04,320
I was considering turning around
to take the initiative.

390
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,230
But sorry. I took your billhook.

391
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:10,360
Then I completely forgot it
back at Kagemori manor.

392
00:17:10,450 --> 00:17:12,780
If you start swinging that thing
around in a crowded city,

393
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:14,620
we'll be in trouble,
so you're all good!

394
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,870
Don't sweat it, kid!

395
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:20,250
Though if you want a weapon,
we could stop by my old pad.

396
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:22,040
I should probably
grab something, too.

397
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:24,500
[YURU] You mean your home?
Is it nearby?

398
00:17:24,590 --> 00:17:25,880
[DERA] Just a short walk.

399
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,210
You wouldn't prefer

400
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:29,460
that we do away
with our tails first?

401
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:31,220
They'll find out where you live.

402
00:17:31,630 --> 00:17:33,470
[DERA]
Oh, they're gonna find out.

403
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:36,060
I was gonna
ditch the place anyway,

404
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:38,270
but let's get some more
use out of it.

405
00:17:46,230 --> 00:17:47,900
It's like a maze here.

406
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:50,070
[DERA] Don't fall behind, kid.

407
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:51,650
You'll get lost.

408
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,120
Taking another turn.

409
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,220
[DERA] In here.

410
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,180
You can keep your shoes on.

411
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,140
[switch clicks]

412
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,520
[Yuru exclaims]

413
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:26,020
Have at it.
Take whatever you want.

414
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:30,070
[Yuru exclaims contentedly]

415
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,940
I sense the presence
of daemons here.

416
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,860
-What?
-I'd hope so.

417
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,580
[MAN 1]
This is Tadera's safehouse?

418
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:44,460
Let's not engage them.
The job's done.

419
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,630
We can report this
to the higher-ups.

420
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:49,590
-[DERA] Leaving so soon?
-[all gasp]

421
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,300
You could at least stay for tea.

422
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,460
[all grunt]

423
00:18:54,970 --> 00:18:56,180
[both grunting]

424
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:00,850
Damn. [pants]

425
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:15,860
[DERA] Welcome, friend,
to the Tadera clan's Lost House.

426
00:19:15,950 --> 00:19:18,780
Barely a thing separates
this world from ours.

427
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:19,910
Unfortunately,

428
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,870
I'm the only one who knows
the route in and out.

429
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:25,250
So for a first-time visitor
like you,

430
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,830
there's no hope for escape.

431
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:30,170
Make even one mistake through
the crazy twists and turns,

432
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,840
and you'll be running in circles
till you fall over dead.

433
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,170
[man grunts]

434
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,970
[MAN] Huh? [screams]

435
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:41,350
[DERA] That's a Kagemori agent
who tailed me once.

436
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,640
You should never follow
a Tadera.

437
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,680
This guy found out why,
as you can see.

438
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:49,020
There are more like him
scattered around.

439
00:19:49,110 --> 00:19:51,020
You don't wanna
wind up like them,

440
00:19:51,110 --> 00:19:53,650
I suggest you
start talkin' real quick.

441
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:55,860
[grunts] Damn it.

442
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:57,360
Oi, Dera!

443
00:19:57,450 --> 00:19:59,990
I still sense the presence
of daemons about here!

444
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:02,330
I'm well aware. Look.

445
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:04,620
Those are my family's daemons.

446
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,370
-[MAN] What?
-[YURU] The house?

447
00:20:06,450 --> 00:20:09,040
This pair can come together
to create a Lost House.

448
00:20:09,130 --> 00:20:10,630
-[both gasp]
-[DERA] It's like Higashi.

449
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,170
-Once you enter--
-[RIGHT] No.

450
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:13,210
Huh?

451
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:15,170
Not those.

452
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:17,380
We sense another pair.

453
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:22,350
[man grunts]

454
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:49,250
[laughing]

455
00:21:09,390 --> 00:21:10,850
[daemon 2 laughing]

456
00:21:20,530 --> 00:21:22,450
[DAEMON 1] Ooh, lookie!

457
00:21:22,530 --> 00:21:25,780
Oh me, oh my, oh me, oh my!

458
00:21:25,870 --> 00:21:29,370
[DAEMON 2] Been a long while,
Left and Right.

459
00:21:29,870 --> 00:21:33,130
[LEFT] Yuru, Dera,
take this one and fall back.

460
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:39,260
[both chuckling]

461
00:21:42,010 --> 00:21:45,760
[RIGHT] Tenaga-Ashinaga,
Long-Arm and Long-Leg.

462
00:21:45,850 --> 00:21:48,390
You're no match
for the likes of them.

463
00:21:48,470 --> 00:21:50,350
[both laughing]

464
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

465
00:23:27,950 --> 00:23:30,240
[Long-Leg yells]

466
00:23:30,330 --> 00:23:32,910
[Long-Arm laughs]

467
00:23:32,990 --> 00:23:36,870
[LONG-ARM AND LONG-LEG]
Damn you all!
